course: dictionary
lesson: 2422
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. The word «cylinder» is a good example. In maths it is a 3D shape, and in science and everyday life it is a tube-shaped container.
explain: «A home fizzy-water machine pushes carbon dioxide from a cylinder into water under high pressure.» Here a cylinder is a container that holds gas. The words gas, pressure and machine are the clues. In a maths lesson, you would read about faces, edges and volume instead.
explain: Phrases can also change a word's meaning. «Not firing on all cylinders» has nothing to do with shapes or gas. It means not thinking clearly, like an engine running badly, and it is often said about someone who is tired or ill.
fact: A cylinder in maths is a 3D shape with two equal flat circles at the ends and one curved side joining them.
fact: A cylinder has 2 flat faces, 1 curved face, 2 curved edges, and no corners.
fact: A cylinder can also be a tube-shaped container, such as a gas cylinder.
fact: «Firing on all cylinders» means working well and thinking clearly.
fact: The adjective from cylinder is cylindrical, as in «a cylindrical tin of beans».
exercise: «A home fizzy-water machine pushes carbon dioxide from a cylinder into water under high pressure.» What is a cylinder in this sentence? | *A tube-shaped container that holds gas | A loud noise | A flat circle with a hole in it | A kind of drink
exercise: Which shape has two equal flat circle ends and one curved side? | A pyramid | *A cylinder | A cube | A sphere
exercise: «He is not firing on all cylinders today.» What does this mean? | He has lost his car keys | *He is not thinking clearly, often because he is tired or ill | He is making a loud noise like an engine | He is running very fast
test: How many flat faces does a cylinder have? | 3 | 0 | 1 | *2
test: Which word is the adjective from cylinder? | cylinderize | *cylindrical | cylinders | cylinderful
exam: «In a petrol engine, fuel burns in small cylinders and pushes pistons, which turn a crankshaft and then the wheels.» What do the cylinders do in this sentence? | Make the car lighter | Stop the wheels from turning | Turn the wheels directly | *Hold burning fuel that pushes the pistons
